{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480185883,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxOTE4MjAzOTM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1144","origin":"github"},"title":"`publish` should switch to `git annex sync --no-pull`","message":"I don't actually know whether the is a problem for the current implementation, but I thought to write it down anyway.\n\n In direct mode, as well as v6 unlocked mode the checked out branch is not the one to be published! We need to make sure to sync all the changes in adjusted branches etc, before we push anything. Likely, we should rely on `git annex sync` instead of any manual `git push` calls whenever possible (plain git needs special treatment).","files":null}]}